title: 'HRMP: New Deposit Flow'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The relay chain HRMP pallet now sets channel deposits through the new `ChannelDeposits` and
    `OnDepositSet` traits from `hrmp-primitives`, set as `hrmp::Config::DepositProvider`. Each call
    asks the provider with a `DepositAction` and the `Deposits` each side should hold, priced from
    the active config. The provider sets and tracks the deposits and reports back through
    `on_deposit_set` with the same `Deposits`, where the call finishes and records what was set, so
    a provider on another chain can finish it later. Init and accept on system channels skip it.
    Dropping an open request on offboarding now also frees the sender's request slot. Force and
    system channel opens now also emit `OpenChannelRequested` and `OpenChannelAccepted`.

    `LocalDepositProvider` reserves and unreserves through `Config::Currency` in the same call.
    Every runtime must now set `type DepositProvider`; `LocalDepositProvider<Runtime>` works as a
    drop-in.

    Prepares for taking deposits in `pallet-hrmp-para` on the Coretime chain (Asset Hub on Kusama).
crates:
- name: hrmp-primitives
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-hrmp-relay
  bump: none
- name: polkadot-sdk-frame
  bump: none
